<title>BRAZIL: Telebras may issue bond in second half.</title>
<headline>Telebras may issue bond in second half.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telebras President Fernando Xavier Ferreira said the federally owned telecoms firm may issue new debt in the second half of this year.</p>
<p>&quot;It may be done in the second half.  Currently the company does not need financing,&quot; Ferreira told reporters.</p>
<p>Ferreira did not say which markets the company would consider tapping.  Other Telebras officials said earlier this year that the company was considering doing a $300 million Yankee bond, but they did not give a time.</p>
<p>((--John Miller, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248-5414))</p>
